</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Temple Mount — Herodian Temple platform</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for the platform; exact episode locations unknown. The surviving retaining walls and archaeological topography securely locate Herod&#x27;s Temple platform. The Gospels associate Jesus with presentation, teaching, festival visits, and actions in the Temple precincts.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for the platform; exact episode locations unknown

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 2:22-38; Luke 2:41-52; Mark 11:11-18; John 7-10

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The surviving retaining walls and archaeological topography securely locate Herod's Temple platform. The Gospels associate Jesus with presentation, teaching, festival visits, and actions in the Temple precincts.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The sanctuary and courts were destroyed in 70 CE. The marker does not claim that the Dome of the Rock, or any other precise point on the platform, was the location of a particular saying or action.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 2:22-38: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+2%3A22-38&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 2:41-52: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+2%3A41-52&version=NRSVUE
- Mark 11:11-18: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+11%3A11-18&version=NRSVUE
- John 7-10: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+7-10&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: Jerusalem coordinates and atlas bibliography: https://www.openbible.info/geo/modern/m66c5b8/jerusalem

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
