</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Southern Temple approaches and steps</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for the Herodian approach; event link is contextual. The monumental stairways and gates on the south side formed a major public approach to the Temple in Jesus&#x27;s time. They provide a defensible spatial setting for pilgrims entering the precincts.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for the Herodian approach; event link is contextual

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 19:45-48; Luke 21:37-38

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The monumental stairways and gates on the south side formed a major public approach to the Temple in Jesus's time. They provide a defensible spatial setting for pilgrims entering the precincts.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
No Gospel specifies which Temple gate or staircase Jesus used. Treat this as an archaeological context marker, not the identified location of a particular sermon.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 19:45-48: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+19%3A45-48&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 21:37-38: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+21%3A37-38&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: Jerusalem coordinates and atlas bibliography: https://www.openbible.info/geo/modern/m66c5b8/jerusalem

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
