</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Pools of Bethesda</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High-to-moderate. Excavations north of the Temple revealed a double-pool complex whose division created a fifth portico, fitting John&#x27;s unusually specific description. The complex existed during the Second Temple period.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High-to-moderate

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 5:1-18

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Excavations north of the Temple revealed a double-pool complex whose division created a fifth portico, fitting John's unusually specific description. The complex existed during the Second Temple period.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The identification is persuasive but not mathematically provable; scholars have proposed other Jerusalem pools, and the exact point of the healing within the complex is unknowable.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 5:1-18: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+5%3A1-18&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Holy Land Photos: Pools of Bethesda: https://holylandphotos.org/browse.asp?s=1%2C2%2C6%2C19%2C378%2C398

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
