</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Second Temple-period Pool of Siloam</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High-to-moderate. A large stepped pool from the relevant period was uncovered at the southern end of the City of David in 2004. Its date, location, and function make it the leading identification for John&#x27;s Pool of Siloam.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High-to-moderate

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 9:1-12

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
A large stepped pool from the relevant period was uncovered at the southern end of the City of David in 2004. Its date, location, and function make it the leading identification for John's Pool of Siloam.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Only part of the pool is exposed, and direct proof tying the specific healing to this structure is impossible. Older visitors were often shown the smaller Byzantine pool farther north.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 9:1-12: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+9%3A1-12&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Holy Land Photos: excavated Second Temple-period Pool of Siloam: https://holylandphotos.org/browse.asp?img=IJOTHT21&s=1%2C2%2C6%2C19%2C97

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
