</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Mount of Olives — ridge and teaching setting</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for the landform; exact teaching point unknown. The ridge east of Jerusalem is an unmistakable geographic feature and is repeatedly named in the Passion narratives. Its western slope overlooks the Temple platform.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for the landform; exact teaching point unknown

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Mark 13:1-37; Luke 21:37; Luke 22:39

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The ridge east of Jerusalem is an unmistakable geographic feature and is repeatedly named in the Passion narratives. Its western slope overlooks the Temple platform.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The pin marks the ridge generally. The Gospels do not supply coordinates for the Olivet discourse, nightly lodging, prayer, or post-resurrection events.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Mark 13:1-37: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+13%3A1-37&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 21:37: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+21%3A37&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 22:39: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+22%3A39&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: Jerusalem coordinates and atlas bibliography: https://www.openbible.info/geo/modern/m66c5b8/jerusalem

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
