</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Kidron Valley — route between city and Mount of Olives</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for the valley; crossing point approximate. John explicitly says Jesus crossed the Kidron before entering a garden. The valley still separates the Temple ridge from the Mount of Olives and constrains the route geographically.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for the valley; crossing point approximate

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 18:1-2; Luke 22:39

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
John explicitly says Jesus crossed the Kidron before entering a garden. The valley still separates the Temple ridge from the Mount of Olives and constrains the route geographically.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The ancient path and exact crossing have changed with erosion, fill, roads, and construction. This marker is a representative crossing, not a preserved footprint.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 18:1-2: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+18%3A1-2&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 22:39: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+22%3A39&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: Jerusalem coordinates and atlas bibliography: https://www.openbible.info/geo/modern/m66c5b8/jerusalem

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
