<Point><coordinates>35.238400,31.777520,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Bethany / al-Eizariya — village area</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for the village identification. Al-Eizariya lies on the eastern slope of the Mount of Olives at the distance from Jerusalem given by John and preserves a long identification with Lazarus and Bethany.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for the village identification

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 11:1-44; John 12:1-8; Mark 11:11-12

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Al-Eizariya lies on the eastern slope of the Mount of Olives at the distance from Jerusalem given by John and preserves a long identification with Lazarus and Bethany.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Confidence in the town does not identify the houses of Mary, Martha, Simon, or Lazarus, nor does it prove that the presently shown tomb is Lazarus's tomb.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 11:1-44: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+11%3A1-44&version=NRSVUE
- John 12:1-8: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+12%3A1-8&version=NRSVUE
- Mark 11:11-12: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+11%3A11-12&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Hebrew University gazetteer: Bethany / el-Eizariya / Lazarion: https://dig.corps-cmhl.huji.ac.il/literary_sources/bethany-el-eizariya-lazarion-2
- Tomb of Lazarus: history and limits of the identification: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Lazarus

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
