<Placemark>
<name>Bethlehem — Church of the Nativity area</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for Bethlehem; moderate-to-low for the exact grotto. Matthew and Luke identify Bethlehem as Jesus&#x27;s birthplace. The present basilica preserves an exceptionally early and continuous Christian location tradition centered on the grotto beneath it.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for Bethlehem; moderate-to-low for the exact grotto

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 2:1-18; Luke 2:1-20

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Matthew and Luke identify Bethlehem as Jesus's birthplace. The present basilica preserves an exceptionally early and continuous Christian location tradition centered on the grotto beneath it.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The Gospels identify the town but do not provide a street or cave. The specific grotto is traditional and cannot be archaeologically demonstrated as the birth room.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 2:1-18: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+2%3A1-18&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 2:1-20: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+2%3A1-20&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Bible Odyssey / HarperCollins Bible Dictionary: Bethlehem: https://www.bibleodyssey.org/dictionary/bethlehem/

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
