<Placemark>
<name>Jericho — Tell es-Sultan and oasis area</name>
<styleUrl>#category-1</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">High for the Jericho oasis; exact streets unknown. The ancient settlement and oasis of Jericho are securely located. The Gospels place the healing of blind beggars and the encounter with Zacchaeus in or near Jericho while Jesus traveled toward Jerusalem.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
High for the Jericho oasis; exact streets unknown

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Mark 10:46-52; Luke 18:35-19:10

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The ancient settlement and oasis of Jericho are securely located. The Gospels place the healing of blind beggars and the encounter with Zacchaeus in or near Jericho while Jesus traveled toward Jerusalem.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Jericho had more than one built center in the Roman period, including Herodian development south of the tell. The pin does not identify Zacchaeus's tree or a precise roadside location.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Mark 10:46-52: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+10%3A46-52&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 18:35-19:10: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+18%3A35-19%3A10&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenStreetMap copyright and ODbL attribution: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
