<Placemark>
<name>Traditional Garden of Gethsemane</name>
<styleUrl>#category-2</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Moderate for the vicinity; low for the exact enclosure. The traditional garden lies across the Kidron on the lower Mount of Olives, matching the Gospel geography. Early Christian memory placed Gethsemane in this vicinity, and archaeology has found activity of the relevant period nearby.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Moderate for the vicinity; low for the exact enclosure

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 26:36-56; Mark 14:32-52; Luke 22:39-53; John 18:1-12

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The traditional garden lies across the Kidron on the lower Mount of Olives, matching the Gospel geography. Early Christian memory placed Gethsemane in this vicinity, and archaeology has found activity of the relevant period nearby.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The exact garden is unknown, and the present enclosure is very small. Ancient Gethsemane may have included a broader olive-growing and processing area on the slope.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 26:36-56: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+26%3A36-56&version=NRSVUE
- Mark 14:32-52: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+14%3A32-52&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 22:39-53: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+22%3A39-53&version=NRSVUE
- John 18:1-12: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+18%3A1-12&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Gethsemane: traditions and archaeological caution: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gethsemane

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
