<Placemark>
<name>Gethsemane grotto / olive-press tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-2</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Traditional; exact connection uncertain. A cave north of the modern garden has a long Christian tradition and may suit the name Gethsemane, commonly related to an oil press. It offers a plausible sheltered feature within the correct landscape.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Traditional; exact connection uncertain

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 18:1-12

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
A cave north of the modern garden has a long Christian tradition and may suit the name Gethsemane, commonly related to an oil press. It offers a plausible sheltered feature within the correct landscape.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Nothing identifies this particular cave in the Gospel text. It should be considered an alternative traditional focus within the Gethsemane area, not proof of the arrest spot.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 18:1-12: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+18%3A1-12&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Gethsemane: traditions and archaeological caution: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gethsemane

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
