<Placemark>
<name>Akeldama / Field of Blood vicinity</name>
<styleUrl>#category-2</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Moderate for the traditional vicinity; low for exact parcel. Christian sources by the time of Eusebius located Akeldama in the Hinnom Valley south of Jerusalem. The area contains ancient burial caves and later structures associated with pilgrim burial.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Moderate for the traditional vicinity; low for exact parcel

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 27:3-10; Acts 1:15-20

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Christian sources by the time of Eusebius located Akeldama in the Hinnom Valley south of Jerusalem. The area contains ancient burial caves and later structures associated with pilgrim burial.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Matthew and Acts explain the name differently and neither gives coordinates. The current monastery and burial building mark a long tradition, but the boundaries of the purchased 'field' are unknown.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 27:3-10: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+27%3A3-10&version=NRSVUE
- Acts 1:15-20: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Acts+1%3A15-20&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Madain Project: Akeldama and its identification history: https://madainproject.com/akeldama

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
