<Placemark>
<name>Qasr al-Yahud — western-bank baptism tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-2</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Moderate for the lower-Jordan vicinity; exact bank unknown. Long-standing pilgrimage tradition places Jesus&#x27;s baptism in the lower Jordan east of Jericho. Qasr al-Yahud is the principal access point on the river&#x27;s western bank.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Moderate for the lower-Jordan vicinity; exact bank unknown

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 3:13-17; Mark 1:9-11; Luke 3:21-22; John 1:28

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Long-standing pilgrimage tradition places Jesus's baptism in the lower Jordan east of Jericho. Qasr al-Yahud is the principal access point on the river's western bank.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The river has shifted and the phrase 'Bethany beyond the Jordan' is disputed. The Gospel accounts identify the Jordan region, not this exact landing or modern platform.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 3:13-17: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+3%3A13-17&version=NRSVUE
- Mark 1:9-11: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+1%3A9-11&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 3:21-22: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+3%3A21-22&version=NRSVUE
- John 1:28: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+1%3A28&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenStreetMap copyright and ODbL attribution: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
