<Placemark>
<name>Al-Maghtas — eastern-bank baptism tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-2</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Moderate for the lower-Jordan vicinity; exact channel unknown. Al-Maghtas preserves Byzantine churches, baptismal installations, and a major tradition on the Jordanian side, making it an important counterpart to Qasr al-Yahud.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Moderate for the lower-Jordan vicinity; exact channel unknown

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 1:28-34

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Al-Maghtas preserves Byzantine churches, baptismal installations, and a major tradition on the Jordanian side, making it an important counterpart to Qasr al-Yahud.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The remains document ancient Christian commemoration, not eyewitness proof of the precise baptism point. Ancient river channels and the location of John's Bethany remain debated.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 1:28-34: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+1%3A28-34&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenStreetMap copyright and ODbL attribution: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
