<Placemark>
<name>Ephraim candidate — Taybeh</name>
<styleUrl>#category-2</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Moderate-to-low. John says Jesus withdrew to a town called Ephraim near the wilderness. Taybeh is a commonly proposed identification northeast of Jerusalem and lies near the transition toward wilderness country.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Moderate-to-low

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 11:54

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
John says Jesus withdrew to a town called Ephraim near the wilderness. Taybeh is a commonly proposed identification northeast of Jerusalem and lies near the transition toward wilderness country.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The identification is not certain; other sites have been proposed, and the marker represents the modern town rather than a known house or first-century street.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 11:54: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+11%3A54&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenStreetMap copyright and ODbL attribution: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
