<Placemark>
<name>Dominus Flevit — traditional place of lament</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Commemorative tradition. The church sits on the Mount of Olives with a direct view of Jerusalem and commemorates Jesus weeping over the city, which Luke places during the approach from the mount.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Commemorative tradition

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 19:41-44

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The church sits on the Mount of Olives with a direct view of Jerusalem and commemorates Jesus weeping over the city, which Luke places during the approach from the mount.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Luke gives no exact stopping point. The modern church identifies a fitting viewpoint, not a location recoverable from the text.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 19:41-44: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+19%3A41-44&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: Jerusalem coordinates and atlas bibliography: https://www.openbible.info/geo/modern/m66c5b8/jerusalem

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
