<Placemark>
<name>Pater Noster / Eleona tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Ancient commemoration; event location unknown. The site continues the Mount of Olives Eleona tradition and commemorates Jesus&#x27;s teaching, especially the Lord&#x27;s Prayer.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Ancient commemoration; event location unknown

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 6:5-15; Luke 11:1-4

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The site continues the Mount of Olives Eleona tradition and commemorates Jesus's teaching, especially the Lord's Prayer.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Matthew locates the prayer within the Sermon on the Mount without naming this ridge, while Luke gives no Mount of Olives location. The association is liturgical rather than geographical proof.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 6:5-15: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+6%3A5-15&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 11:1-4: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+11%3A1-4&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: Jerusalem coordinates and atlas bibliography: https://www.openbible.info/geo/modern/m66c5b8/jerusalem

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
