<Placemark>
<name>Cenacle — traditional Upper Room</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Important tradition; existing room medieval. A long tradition places the Last Supper and later gatherings on southwestern Mount Zion. The location became a major focus of Christian memory.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Important tradition; existing room medieval

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Mark 14:12-26; Luke 22:7-38; Acts 1:12-14; Acts 2:1-4

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
A long tradition places the Last Supper and later gatherings on southwestern Mount Zion. The location became a major focus of Christian memory.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The standing hall is medieval, the Gospels do not name the owner or quarter, and reconstructing continuity beneath the present building is disputed. It is not an intact first-century room.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Mark 14:12-26: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+14%3A12-26&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 22:7-38: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+22%3A7-38&version=NRSVUE
- Acts 1:12-14: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Acts+1%3A12-14&version=NRSVUE
- Acts 2:1-4: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Acts+2%3A1-4&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Biblical Archaeology Society: Hunting for the Upper Room: https://www.biblicalarchaeology.org/daily/biblical-sites-places/jerusalem/hunting-for-the-upper-room-in-jerusalem/

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
