<Placemark>
<name>St Mark&#x27;s Syriac Monastery — alternative Upper Room tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Alternative ecclesiastical tradition. Syriac tradition identifies this site with the house of Mary, mother of John Mark, and the Upper Room. It demonstrates that more than one Jerusalem community preserved a localization.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Alternative ecclesiastical tradition

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Mark 14:12-26; Acts 12:12

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Syriac tradition identifies this site with the house of Mary, mother of John Mark, and the Upper Room. It demonstrates that more than one Jerusalem community preserved a localization.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Acts 12 names Mary's house but does not equate it with the Last Supper room. The identification cannot be independently established.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Mark 14:12-26: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+14%3A12-26&version=NRSVUE
- Acts 12:12: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Acts+12%3A12&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Biblical Archaeology Society: Hunting for the Upper Room: https://www.biblicalarchaeology.org/daily/biblical-sites-places/jerusalem/hunting-for-the-upper-room-in-jerusalem/

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
