<Placemark>
<name>St Peter in Gallicantu — Caiaphas-house tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Plausible district; exact house unproved. The church stands in the Upper City/Mount Zion area where elite priestly residences are plausible and commemorates Jesus before Caiaphas and Peter&#x27;s denial.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Plausible district; exact house unproved

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 26:57-75; Luke 22:54-71; John 18:12-27

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The church stands in the Upper City/Mount Zion area where elite priestly residences are plausible and commemorates Jesus before Caiaphas and Peter's denial.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The excavated remains do not name Caiaphas, and the underground chamber is not demonstrably Jesus's prison. Another Caiaphas tradition exists nearby at St Saviour.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 26:57-75: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+26%3A57-75&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 22:54-71: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+22%3A54-71&version=NRSVUE
- John 18:12-27: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+18%3A12-27&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Wikidata: St Peter in Gallicantu location: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1861408

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
