<Placemark>
<name>Armenian St Saviour — alternative Caiaphas tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Alternative medieval tradition. Armenian tradition locates the house of Caiaphas here, close to the Upper City and the better-known Gallicantu tradition.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Alternative medieval tradition

RELEVANT PASSAGES
John 18:13-28

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Armenian tradition locates the house of Caiaphas here, close to the Upper City and the better-known Gallicantu tradition.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The tradition is late and no archaeological evidence ties a recovered building to Caiaphas. Its value is chiefly as evidence that the exact house location is unresolved.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- John 18:13-28: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+18%3A13-28&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Madain Project: Armenian Convent of Saint Saviour: https://madainproject.com/armenian_convent_of_saint_saviour

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
