<Placemark>
<name>Monastery of St Onuphrius — Akeldama commemoration</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Traditional monument within likely Akeldama vicinity. The monastery occupies the southern Hinnom slope amid ancient tombs and marks the long Akeldama tradition.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Traditional monument within likely Akeldama vicinity

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 27:3-10; Acts 1:15-20

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The monastery occupies the southern Hinnom slope amid ancient tombs and marks the long Akeldama tradition.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The monastery is not the field purchased in the first century, and claims about a precise place where Judas died cannot be reconciled securely from Matthew and Acts.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 27:3-10: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+27%3A3-10&version=NRSVUE
- Acts 1:15-20: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Acts+1%3A15-20&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Madain Project: Akeldama and its identification history: https://madainproject.com/akeldama

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
