<Placemark>
<name>Greek Orthodox Shepherds&#x27; Field — alternative</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Alternative regional tradition. This pin is placed on the Greek Orthodox Shepherds&#x27; Field church and monastery, the location shown to visitors as the Orthodox traditional site. It is another ancient Christian focus east of Bethlehem, illustrating that the event belongs to a landscape rather than an identifiable historical parcel.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Alternative regional tradition

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 2:8-20

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
This pin is placed on the Greek Orthodox Shepherds' Field church and monastery, the location shown to visitors as the Orthodox traditional site. It is another ancient Christian focus east of Bethlehem, illustrating that the event belongs to a landscape rather than an identifiable historical parcel.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
No evidence chooses this site over the Catholic field or other nearby grazing land. The marker documents the alternative tradition.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 2:8-20: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+2%3A8-20&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Bible Odyssey / HarperCollins Bible Dictionary: Bethlehem: https://www.bibleodyssey.org/dictionary/bethlehem/
- Greek Orthodox Shepherds' Field church and mapped coordinates: https://www.octagonproject.org/news/the-orthodox-shepherds%E2%80%99-field

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
