<Placemark>
<name>Ein Karem — St John Ba Harim tradition</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Strong later tradition; biblical town unnamed. The church commemorates the birth of John the Baptist in Ein Karem, a long-standing Christian identification west of Jerusalem.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Strong later tradition; biblical town unnamed

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 1:5-25; Luke 1:57-80

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The church commemorates the birth of John the Baptist in Ein Karem, a long-standing Christian identification west of Jerusalem.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
Luke says only that Zechariah and Elizabeth lived in a town in Judea's hill country. It never names Ein Karem, and the precise birthplace is not recoverable.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 1:5-25: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+1%3A5-25&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 1:57-80: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+1%3A57-80&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- Church of the Visitation and the non-specific wording of Luke: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_the_Visitation

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
