<Placemark>
<name>Mount of Temptation — traditional wilderness site</name>
<styleUrl>#category-3</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Traditional; exact wilderness location unspecified. The dramatic cliff west of Jericho has a long monastic tradition connecting it with Jesus&#x27;s temptation after baptism and fits the Judean wilderness landscape.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Traditional; exact wilderness location unspecified

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Matthew 4:1-11; Mark 1:12-13; Luke 4:1-13

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
The dramatic cliff west of Jericho has a long monastic tradition connecting it with Jesus's temptation after baptism and fits the Judean wilderness landscape.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The Gospels name only the wilderness and do not identify a mountain beside Jericho. The monastery marks a devotional tradition, not a textually fixed site.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Matthew 4:1-11: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+4%3A1-11&version=NRSVUE
- Mark 1:12-13: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Mark+1%3A12-13&version=NRSVUE
- Luke 4:1-13: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+4%3A1-13&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenStreetMap copyright and ODbL attribution: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
