<Folder><name>4 — Emmaus: competing identifications</name><open>0</open><visibility>0</visibility>
<Placemark>
<name>Emmaus candidate — Qalunya / Motza</name>
<styleUrl>#category-4</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Leading distance-based candidate; disputed. Qalunya/Motza lies close to the approximately sixty-stadia distance found in most manuscripts of Luke and has an ancient settlement context west of Jerusalem.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Leading distance-based candidate; disputed

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 24:13-35

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Qalunya/Motza lies close to the approximately sixty-stadia distance found in most manuscripts of Luke and has an ancient settlement context west of Jerusalem.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
No consensus exists. Identifying the Gospel village with Motza depends on name-history and distance arguments that do not provide a decisive match.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 24:13-35: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+24%3A13-35&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: six proposed identifications of Emmaus: https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/ae7274b/emmaus

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
