</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Emmaus candidate — Nicopolis</name>
<styleUrl>#category-4</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Ancient identification; distance-text problem. Emmaus Nicopolis has the strongest surviving ancient place-name and became the principal Byzantine identification.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Ancient identification; distance-text problem

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 24:13-35

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Emmaus Nicopolis has the strongest surviving ancient place-name and became the principal Byzantine identification.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
It is roughly 160 rather than 60 stadia from Jerusalem. A minority textual variant reads 160, but the longer same-day walking narrative is difficult and the manuscript evidence is contested.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 24:13-35: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+24%3A13-35&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: six proposed identifications of Emmaus: https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/ae7274b/emmaus

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
