</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Emmaus candidate — Abu Ghosh</name>
<styleUrl>#category-4</styleUrl>
<Snippet maxLines="4">Crusader tradition; disputed. Crusaders identified Abu Ghosh with Emmaus and built a substantial church there; its location on the westward road made it a persuasive pilgrimage station.</Snippet>
<description><![CDATA[ASSESSMENT
Crusader tradition; disputed

RELEVANT PASSAGES
Luke 24:13-35

WHY THE MARKER IS HERE
Crusaders identified Abu Ghosh with Emmaus and built a substantial church there; its location on the westward road made it a persuasive pilgrimage station.

WHAT REMAINS UNCERTAIN
The tradition is much later than the Gospel and the distance does not resolve the competing proposals. It should not be presented as the certain Emmaus.

SCRIPTURE LINKS
- Luke 24:13-35: https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke+24%3A13-35&version=NRSVUE

REFERENCES
- OpenBible.info: six proposed identifications of Emmaus: https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/ae7274b/emmaus

Coordinates mark a modern site or representative point; they do not claim centimeter-level location of an ancient event.]]></description>
