<Folder><name>6 — Read me and source method</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>Start here — evidence and certainty</name>
<description><![CDATA[<h2>How to interpret this map</h2><p><b>Strong geographic identification</b> means the town, pool, valley, ridge, or monumental platform is reasonably identifiable. It does not prove that a particular event occurred on the pin.</p><p><b>Plausible</b> means geography, archaeology, and/or early tradition make the vicinity defensible, while an exact location remains unproved.</p><p><b>Later tradition or alternative</b> documents an important pilgrimage identification but should not be confused with archaeological demonstration.</p><p>Biblical citations identify the narrative basis. External references explain geographical or archaeological reasoning. Coordinates use modern map data and are intended for visualization.</p>]]></description>
<Point><coordinates>35.23417,31.77667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
